hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22854","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Muawiyah narrated to us, from Damrah ibn Habib, that Ibn Zughb al-Iyadi narrated to him, who said: Abdullah ibn Hawalah al-Azdi stayed with me, and indeed he was staying with me in my house. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us around Medina on our feet to take spoils, so we returned and did not take any spoils, and he recognized hardship in our faces, so he stood among us and said: O Allah, do not entrust them to me lest I be weak, and do not entrust them to themselves lest they be incapable of it, and do not entrust them to people lest they prefer themselves over them. Then he said: Sham and Rome and Persia, or: Rome and Persia, will be opened for you, until one of you will have such-and-such of camels, and such-and-such of cattle, and of sheep, until one of them will be given a hundred dinars and will be angry at it. Then he placed his hand on my head, or my crown, and said: O Ibn Hawalah, when you see the caliphate has descended on the sacred land, then earthquakes and calamities and great matters have drawn near, and the Hour that day is nearer to people than these two hands of mine are to your head."
"22855","Hajjaj narrated to us: Layth narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Rabiah ibn Laqit at-Tujibi, from Abdullah ibn Hawalah al-Azdi, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever is saved from three has been saved, saying it three times. They said: What, O Messenger of Allah? He said: My death, and being killed by a rightly steadfast caliph giving it its due, and the Dajjal."
"22856","Isam ibn Khalid and Ali ibn Ayyash said: Hariz narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Sumayr, from Ibn Hawalah al-Azdi, and he was of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: There will be enlisted armies: Sham and Yemen and Iraq, and Allah knows with which of them He began. And upon you is Sham; lo, upon you is Sham; lo, upon you is Sham. So whoever dislikes it, upon him is his Yemen, and let him water in his ponds, for indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, has guaranteed for me Sham and its people."
